CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ narrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ char16_t: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.prim.literal]/1, [lex.string]/6, [dcl.type.decltype]/1.5:
decltype("a") is const char (&)[2] and decltype(u"ab") const char16_t
(&)[3].  __is_same compared the array types structurally, so an array
whose const was recorded on the array node ([basic.type.qualifier]/3)
differed from one whose elements were const, and decltype did not treat
a wide string literal (an array constant) as the lvalue it is (bin53).
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
